{"comment": "Document sync into the daemon's overlays (plan §2.5, §4.4). An open document whose text differs from the disk is answered ContentModified (-32801), not from the disk, whether it is the document asked about or one the answer points into (here greet/Greeter.java, open with a line inserted, holding the definition of a name asked about in Main.java): the index holds the disk's text, so a location there would be placed in a text the client does not have. A ranged didChange (here: the first line deleted) is applied to the session's copy and sent whole with its version, so once the text equals the disk the definition is answered. A change whose range does not fit the text, or whose version does not increase, parts the document from the session: every request on it is ContentModified until it is opened again."}
